What the Indigo Hammer revealed about Z

A child finishing the missing “O” in Old MacDonald demonstrates constrained completion. A child inventing an entirely new verse after being offered the space is a candidate for catalytic silence. To establish causation, we would still need comparison and replication.

That’s a meaningful refinement: we don’t award Z just because something happened after a pause.

